cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software and the accompanying
  paper (preferred-citation).
type: software
title: "vfates: Same Rate, Different Fates"
abstract: >-
  Step-zero screen for when verifier errors transfer in RL with verifiable
  rewards. The code tests, in a preregistered design across five task domains
  (arithmetic, competition math, code, instruction following and judged QA),
  model sizes from 1.7B to 32B and three model families, whether resampled
  noise, prompt-specific errors, and errors carried by a shared behaviour lead
  to different held-out outcomes at matched step-0 false-positive and
  false-negative rates, whether transfer precision, estimated and locked
  before training from a few hundred oracle labels, orders those outcomes, and
  whether it chooses better verifier fixes than the error count.
